{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling: ChatGPT card-frame origin when no frame exists before consent\n\nStep 5 of docs/o4-connect.md asks you to record the ChatGPT card frame's origin before consent. ChatGPT shows a card only after a tool call, and a tool call needs a connected connector. So expect no frame before consent. This ruling settles that case in advance.\n\n1. Before consent, look once for any ChatGPT frame that loads dap content. If one exists, record its origin. If it equals https://dap-connect.inguz.workers.dev, stop before consent and report.\n2. If no frame exists, record that limit and continue with consent as @o4-member. The grant goes to one agent and is revocable.\n3. At the first ChatGPT card render, record the frame's actual origin before any press, call or other interaction with the card.\n4. If that origin equals https://dap-connect.inguz.workers.dev, press nothing in the card. Revoke the ChatGPT grant from the consent page at once, confirm that the next ChatGPT call fails with 401, and report. Claude's scene stays valid. I then rule on ChatGPT's card domain before any retry.\n5. If the origin differs from the Worker origin, continue the ChatGPT scene as written.\n\nReason: the member's browser key lives at the Worker origin. A card frame on that origin would share its storage, and the guard is to never interact with such a frame. The grant's revocation bounds the time a consented connector exists before the check.\n\nDeployment note: 0455c637 changes the Question card for every host. Before the live window I redeploy dap-connect from 0455c637 or later, closed, then open it. The three existing Workers stay on bcf88654 with MCP closed; they take 0455c637 at their next planned deployment.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}